  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFrom this test page: https://codepen.io/sb3nder/pen/EaWadPv?editors=1100\n\nUAs `<select>` validity differs from the spec mainly in these 3 cases:\n\n- for `<select multiple size=1>` when the placeholder option is selected (this is a recent change... #12246).\n```html\n<select required multiple size=\"1\">\n\t<option value=\"\" selected>placeholder</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n- An empty `<optgroup>` before the placeholder option.\n```html\n<select required>\n\t<optgroup label=\"group\"></optgroup>\n\t<option value=\"\">placeholder</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n- Wrapper elements around `<option>` #12892.\n```html\n<select required>\n\t<div>\n\t\t<option value=\"\">placeholder</option>\n\t</div>\n</select>\n```",
